<item><title>Gambians vote December 5 as Barrow seeks a third term</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambians-vote-december-5-as-barrow-seeks-a-third-term-7d693c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambians-vote-december-5-as-barrow-seeks-a-third-term-7d693c/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The election pits the president against opposition leader Ousainou Darboe and six other candidates, with presidential term limits still absent from the constitution.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:31:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambians-vote-december-5-as-barrow-seeks-a-third-term-7d693c/share.jpg" length="41103" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambians-vote-december-5-as-barrow-seeks-a-third-term-7d693c/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Bensouda challenges reported D4.9 billion vehicle spending</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/bensouda-challenges-reported-d4-9-billion-vehicle-spending-710672/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/bensouda-challenges-reported-d4-9-billion-vehicle-spending-710672/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The presidential candidate said rural communities need better services and pledged to redirect public resources and improve farmers’ access to finance.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:14:27 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gambian journalist Mustapha K. Darboe wins Abuja investigative journalism award</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambian-journalist-mustapha-k-darboe-wins-abuja-f93ce6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambian-journalist-mustapha-k-darboe-wins-abuja-f93ce6/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>Darboe was recognised for a report on a multi-million-dollar Gambian government venture that made the President&apos;s nephew a major food importer.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:13:31 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>EFF leader promises airline and D8 million Kiang mill if Darboe wins</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/eff-leader-promises-airline-and-d8-million-kiang-mill-if-d1bf2f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/eff-leader-promises-airline-and-d8-million-kiang-mill-if-d1bf2f/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>Prince Ebrahim Sanyang says he will launch an airline within 30 days of a Darboe victory and donate D100,000 to youth sports.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:18:51 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
